  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Jamaican Dominoes. 4 players, Double-Six dominoes. Modes: Partner (2v2) or Cut-Throat (4 individuals). Setup: 7 tiles per player, boneyard. Play: Match tile ends. Draw if no legal play. Scoring: Pips in won tricks. Win: First to 100+ points.',
    Player: "Welcome to Jamaican Dominoes. Play with partners or all-against-all (cut-throat). Match the ends of dominoes on the chain. When you can't play, draw from the boneyard. Score points for pips in tricks you win. First to 100 points and their partner/team wins the match.",
    objective: 'In Partner: your team aims to win 6 points while the opponents have 0 (six love). In Cut Throat: be first to 6 wins provided another player has 0. Win a hand by playing all your bones or by having fewest spots when the game is blocked.',
    gameplay: 'Play is anti-clockwise. Each turn a player plays one bone to extend one of the two ends of the layout; touching ends must match. Doubles are played at right angles. If a player cannot play they pass (no draw in standard block style for Partner; Cut Throat follows same play). The hand ends when one player empties their hand or the game blocks. Winning team scores 1 point; playing the key bone (only playable bone when both ends are hard) scores 2.',
    keyRules: [
      'Partner or cut-throat',
      '7 bones each',
      'key bone scores 2',
      'six love to win',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Four players for Partner or Cut Throat; partners sit opposite at a square table.',
      deck: 'Double-six domino set of 28 tiles (0-0 through 6-6), known as bones.',
      equipment: 'Tiles',
      dealing: 'Each player receives 7 bones; in Cut Throat with 4 players each gets 7; remaining tiles form the boneyard.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Play is anti-clockwise. Each turn a player plays one bone to extend one of the two ends of the layout; touching ends must match. Doubles are played at right angles. If a player cannot play they pass (no draw in standard block style for Partner; Cut Throat follows same play). The hand ends when one player empties their hand or the game blocks. Winning team scores 1 point; playing the key bone (only playable bone when both ends are hard) scores 2.',
